### Demo 2 — Azure SQL with Entra ID
### Two tokens: one for a reader, one for a broker. Acquire them before the session.
@host  = http://localhost:5000
@reader = Bearer eyJ...            # paste a token whose roles claim contains "reader"
@broker = Bearer eyJ...            # paste a token whose roles claim contains "broker"

### anonymous — with EntraId configured and no anonymous permissions, this is a 403
GET {{host}}/api/policies

### reader — all rows, but commission_amount is absent from the payload
GET {{host}}/api/policies
Authorization: {{reader}}

### broker — fewer rows: the item-level policy became a predicate in the query
GET {{host}}/api/policies
Authorization: {{broker}}

### broker — allowed to update only two columns
PATCH {{host}}/api/policies/id/1
Authorization: {{broker}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "active", "expiry_date": "2028-01-14" }

### broker — this one fails: premium is not in the allowed field list
PATCH {{host}}/api/policies/id/1
Authorization: {{broker}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "premium": 1.00 }

### permission-aware OpenAPI (2.0) — development mode only
GET {{host}}/api/openapi
GET {{host}}/api/openapi/reader
GET {{host}}/api/openapi/broker

### cache: run twice within the TTL and watch the database, not the browser
GET {{host}}/api/policies?$filter=status eq 'active'
Authorization: {{reader}}
